cloud Computing vs. Traditional Networks

Cloud computing utilizes remote servers and services hosted on the internet, offering an alternative to traditional on-premise networks where companies own and maintain their network devices.
This shift allows organizations to access network resources and data from remote data centers via the internet, rather than housing servers at their physical location.
Benefits of Cloud Networking

Companies can save money and streamline network operations by using third-party cloud providers, as they only pay for the storage and processing power they need.
Cloud networks provide the advantages of a traditional network without the need for companies to store devices or manage the network themselves.
The Rise of Cloud Security

As more organizations migrate to cloud services, cloud security is becoming a crucial aspect of network security.
Security professionals now need to focus on verifying both the origin of network traffic and the identity associated with it, moving beyond traditional network-based solutions.
